<title>IRAQ: Iraq reiterates not to export until aid plan passed.</title>
<headline>Iraq reiterates not to export until aid plan passed.</headline>
<dateline>BAGHDAD 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq reiterated it will not export oil under its oil-for-food deal with the United Nations until the U.N. has approved its new aid distribution plan, Iraqi News Agency INA said in a dispatch from New York.</p>
<p>INA quoted Iraq's U.N. ambassador Nizar Hamdoun as saying that the submission of the plan was delayed because of the slow of work demonstrated by the U.N. body which was consulting with Iraq to prepare the plan.</p>
</text>
